  "final_message": "Implemented all three versions:\n\n- [Rust](C:/Users/sandh/nb-work/39-rust-vs-python/sessions/terra/align/rust/src/main.rs) uses a single dynamic-programming row and precomputed substitution costs.\n- [plain.py](C:/Users/sandh/nb-work/39-rust-vs-python/sessions/terra/align/plain.py) uses the same rolling-row algorithm with precomputed costs.\n- [fast.py](C:/Users/sandh/nb-work/39-rust-vs-python/sessions/terra/align/fast.py) uses NumPy cumulative minima to compute each row with array operations.\n\nEach version uses the shorter string for the row width, transposing costs when needed. All three pass samples **s1, s2, and s3**, and an additional 200 randomized cases checked against an independent recurrence. The Rust release build succeeded offline.",
